e":"Senior Electrical Engineer | AGILE Position 1022","metaDescription":"Senior Electrical Engineer in Chadds Ford, PA. Hybrid Schedule. Salary $130,000 to $155,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1023","responsibilities":"• Serve as Project Engineer for electrical engineering assignments\n• Ensure coordination across all design disciplines\n• Contribute to project estimation, scheduling, and constructability analysis\n• Develop electrical design drawings and specifications\n• Conduct site investigations and engineering studies\n• Provide technical input during construction and respond to RFIs\n• Represent the firm at project meetings and client interactions\n• Monitor project production and ensure adherence to schedule and budget\n• Participate in quality assurance and technical reviews of deliverables\n• Maintain documentation and meeting minutes\n• Coordinate with internal design teams and external client reps\n• Address and resolve project-related issues during design and construction\n• Support project scope, schedule, and cost development\n• Ensure production aligns with company quality standards","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s degree in Electrical Engineering from an ABET-accredited university\n• Professional Engineer (PE) license – Required\n• Active NCEES account – Required\n• Minimum 10 years of relevant electrical design experience\n• PMP Certification – Preferred\n• Proficiency in AutoCAD, Revit, and Microsoft Office\n• Strong working knowledge of electrical codes and design standards\n• Excellent written and verbal communication skills\n• Ability to manage and prioritize multiple deadlines\n• Collaborative mindset with a strong sense of accountability\n• Familiarity with MEP, fire alarm, and low voltage/ICT systems\n• Experience working on complex public sector and institutional projects","whyConsider":"Bring your electrical engineering expertise to impactful projects—and grow your career in a collaborative, respected firm.\nAvailable now.","seoTitle":"Electrical Project Engineer | AGILE Position 1023","metaDescription":"Electrical Project Engineer in Chadds Ford, PA. Hybrid Schedule. Salary $120,000 to $155,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1024","responsibilities":"• Prepare electrical design drawings, specifications, and reports.\n• Perform lighting calculations and arc flash studies.\n• Conduct field investigations to document existing conditions.\n• Oversee project construction phases, including submittal reviews, site observation, and punch list reports.\n• Collaborate with mechanical, civil, structural engineers, and architects using AutoCAD/Revit.\n• Support projects with technical analysis, modeling, and reporting.","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s degree in Electrical Engineering.\n• Minimum 5 years of engineering experience involving building systems projects.\n• Experience with power distribution, lighting, fire alarm, security, and telecom systems.\n• Proficiency in Revit, AutoCAD, MS Excel, and Word.\n• Familiarity with AGi32 lighting software, SKM power analysis software, and Arc Flash evaluation.\n• Strong writing, organizational, and communication skills.\n• Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously.\n• On path toward New York P.E. license preferred (not required).","whyConsider":"• Real field work: existing-conditions investigations, arc flash studies and lighting design, not just drafting.\n• Healthcare, campus and institutional projects in the Capital Region.\n• Room to grow into senior electrical and project leadership.\n• A strong focus on professional development, with structured learning, mentorship and knowledge sharing.\n• Exposure to high-performance, sustainable building design and decarbonization work.\n• Benefits: 401(k), health insurance, paid time off, life and disability coverage, and support for EIT and PE licensure.","seoTitle":"Electrical Engineer | AGILE Position 1024","metaDescription":"Electrical Engineer in Albany, NY. Hybrid. Salary $75,000 to $105,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1025","responsibilities":"• Lead electrical engineering for multi-discipline projects through proposal, design, bidding, and construction phases.\n• Interact closely with mechanical, civil, and structural engineers, as well as project architects.\n• Perform code reviews and ensure compliance across project deliverables.\n• Delegate and monitor project tasks for junior team members.\n• Conduct building condition assessments and prepare technical reports.\n• Represent the firm in meetings with internal and external clients.\n• Develop design concepts, strategies, drawings, specifications, and reports.","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s degree in Electrical Engineering (required).\n• Minimum 10 years of experience with an A/E consulting firm (required).\n• New York State Professional Engineer (P.E.) license preferred.\n• Experience with electrical distribution systems, power, lighting, utilities, communications, security, and fire alarm systems.\n• AutoCAD and Revit experience is a plus.\n• Strong leadership, organizational, and communication skills.\n• Ability to work independently and as part of multi-discipline teams.","whyConsider":"• Lead electrical engineering on multi-discipline energy and utility projects from proposal through construction.\n• Work shoulder to shoulder with mechanical, civil and structural engineers.\n• Technical authority on code reviews and compliance across every deliverable.\n• Continuous learning is built in: mentorship, in-house training and knowledge sharing across teams.\n• Work alongside in-house sustainability, technology and commissioning expertise.\n• A full benefits package: 401(k), health, life and disability insurance, paid time off, and EIT/PE licensure support.","seoTitle":"Senior Electrical Engineer | AGILE Position 1025","metaDescription":"Senior Electrical Engineer in Albany, NY. Hybrid. Salary $100,000 to $130,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1026","responsibilities":"• Prepare electrical design drawings, specifications, and technical reports.\n• Perform lighting calculations and arc flash studies.\n• Conduct field investigations to document existing conditions.\n• Support project construction phases, including submittal reviews, site observation, and punch lists.\n• Collaborate with mechanical, civil, structural engineers, and architects using Revit/AutoCAD.\n• Provide technical support across a variety of building system projects.","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s degree in Electrical Engineering required.\n• Minimum 5 years of engineering experience with building systems projects.\n• Proven experience with power distribution, lighting, fire alarm, security, and telecommunications systems.\n• Proficiency in Revit, AutoCAD, MS Excel, and Word.\n• Familiarity with AGi32 (lighting), SKM (power), and Arc-Flash evaluation.\n• Strong writing, organizational, and communication skills.\n• Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously.\n• On path toward New York P.E. license preferred, not required.","whyConsider":"• Work that matters: electric bus charging for a major transit agency, hospitals, campuses, power generation and public facilities.\n• Engineering and construction management under one roof, so you see projects built, not just drawn.\n• Arc flash, lighting and field investigation experience that grows a well-rounded electrical engineer.\n• A firm built for the future of e-mobility and energy, with 30+ years of stability behind it.\n• Comprehensive benefits, including a 401(k), health insurance, PTO, life and disability insurance, and EIT and PE licensure support.","seoTitle":"Electrical Engineer | AGILE Position 1026","metaDescription":"Electrical Engineer in Albany, NY. Hybrid. Salary $75,000 to $105,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1027","responsibilities":"• Lead and oversee electrical engineering projects through all phases: program, schematic, design development, construction documents, bidding, and construction.\n• Independently evaluate, select, and adapt engineering techniques and procedures to meet project requirements.\n• Collaborate with Principals, Associates, and Project Managers to finalize project scope, schedules, and deliverables.\n• Supervise, coordinate, and review work of engineers and designers, assigning tasks to meet deadlines.\n• Prepare reports, studies, and system analyses.\n• Review and recommend substitute equipment, and evaluate final system adjustments after installation.\n• Represent the firm at client meetings, coordinating across all trades.\n• Mentor and train junior engineers and designers to build technical and leadership capacity.\n• Provide input to improve design standards and project delivery.","qualifications":"• Bachelor of Science in Electrical Engineering or equivalent.\n• Professional Engineer (P.E.) license preferred; E.I.T. working toward licensure considered.\n• Minimum 8 years of electrical engineering experience, including responsibility for project design.\n• Proven ability to manage project teams, client relationships, and complex technical challenges.\n• Strong leadership and communication skills with mentoring experience.","whyConsider":"• Lead electrical projects through every phase, from program to construction.\n• Independent technical judgment, with principals and associates who listen.\n• Senior-level responsibility based in Buffalo.\n• Variety you won't get everywhere: healthcare, higher education, commercial, and institutional projects, all under one roof.\n• Benefits include a 401(k), health insurance, paid time off, life and disability insurance, and EIT and PE licensure support.","seoTitle":"Senior Electrical Engineer | AGILE Position 1027","metaDescription":"Senior Electrical Engineer in Buffalo, NY. Hybrid. Salary $88,000 to $122,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1028","responsibilities":"• Lead electrical engineering for multi-discipline projects from proposal through construction.\n• Complete electrical designs, including single-line diagrams, panel sizing, electrical room layouts, lighting, and building systems.\n• Perform load calculations for generators, transformers, switchgear, MCCs, VFDs, feeders, and branch circuits.\n• Prepare electrical design drawings, specifications, and technical reports.\n• Review drawings, conduct code compliance checks, and ensure adherence to national, state, and local regulations.\n• Research, develop, and present coordinated design solutions.\n• Conduct field investigations and building condition assessments.\n• Serve as Engineer-of-Record and internal technical design expert on assigned projects.\n• Mentor junior engineers, delegate project tasks, and provide leadership in staff development.\n• Collaborate with architects, contractors, permitting authorities, and industry organizations.\n• Manage projects as both lead engineer and project manager for building engineering-led efforts.","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s or Associate’s degree in Electrical Engineering or related field required.\n• New York State Professional Engineer (PE) license required.\n• 15+ years of experience with an A/E consulting firm.\n• Proven experience with power distribution, lighting, fire alarm, security, and telecom system design.\n• Familiarity with AGi32 (lighting), SKM (power analysis), and Arc-Flash evaluation.\n• Proficiency with AutoCAD and Revit preferred.\n• Strong organizational, communication, and leadership skills.\n• Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously.","whyConsider":"• This is an urgent hire, and we are scheduling confidential interviews now.\n• Step into a true technical leadership role as Engineer-of-Record on a diverse building portfolio, with incentive compensation and a path to firm ownership.\n• Plenty of work ahead: a healthy backlog of projects keeps teams busy and growing.\n• Benefits: 401(k), health insurance, paid time off, life and disability coverage, and support for EIT and PE licensure.","seoTitle":"Senior Electrical Engineer – Buildings | AGILE Position 1028","metaDescription":"Senior Electrical Engineer – Buildings in Buffalo, NY. Hybrid. 15+ years of experience, NYS PE required. Salary $120,000 to $165,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1029","seoTitle":"Senior Electrical Engineer – Healthcare – Buffalo, NY | AGILE Position 1029","metaDescription":"Senior Electrical Engineer (Healthcare) in Buffalo, NY. Hybrid schedule. 10+ years of MEP electrical engineering experience in healthcare building systems. Salary $125,000 to $165,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE.","responsibilities":"Project Development & Client Engagement\n• Scope projects and prepare proposals.\n• Serve as lead electrical engineer on multi-discipline projects from proposal through construction.\n• Build and maintain client relationships across the healthcare sector.\n• Act as project manager for building engineering-led projects.\nElectrical Engineering & Design\n• Develop electrical designs including single-line diagrams, electrical room layouts, panel sizing, and building systems.\n• Perform load calculations for generators, transformers, switchgear, MCCs, panel boards, feeders, and branch circuits.\n• Prepare electrical design drawings, specifications, and reports.\n• Ensure compliance with national, state, and local codes, including FGI guidelines and DOH requirements.\n• Conduct building condition assessments and provide technical reports.\nTeam Collaboration & Leadership\n• Work closely with mechanical, structural, civil engineers, and architects.\n• Mentor and train junior engineers; delegate and review project tasks.\n• Represent the firm with clients, contractors, and permitting authorities.\nTechnical Expertise & Innovation\n• Serve as Engineer-of-Record on assigned projects.\n• Stay current with industry trends, technologies, and best practices.\n• Provide technical solutions through close engagement with manufacturers and contractors.","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s or Associate’s degree in Electrical Engineering or Engineering Technology.\n• Professional Engineer (P.E.) license (NY or OH) strongly preferred.\n• Minimum 10 years of experience with an A/E consulting firm.\n• Proven expertise in power distribution, lighting, fire alarm, security, and telecommunications design.\n• Familiarity with AutoCAD, Revit, AGi32, SKM, and Arc-Flash evaluation.\n• Strong communication, organizational, and leadership skills.\n• Ability to manage multiple projects and deliver quality outcomes.","whyConsider":"• We will walk you through the role, privately and without pressure.\n• If you’re a Senior Electrical Engineer passionate about healthcare design and ready to take on a leadership role, we invite you to apply today for consideration.\n• A diverse mix of healthcare and commercial projects keeps the work interesting and your skills growing.\n• Exposure to high-performance, sustainable building design and decarbonization work.\n• A strong focus on professional development, with structured learning, mentorship and knowledge sharing.\n• A full benefits package: 401(k), health, life and disability insurance, paid time off, and EIT/PE licensure support."},{"id":"1030","responsibilities":"• Develop electrical designs for power distribution, lighting, telecommunications, fire alarm, and security systems.\n• Perform load calculations for generators, transformers, switchgear, panel boards, VFDs, feeders, and branch circuits.\n• Prepare electrical design drawings, specifications, and engineering reports.\n• Assist with building condition assessments and system evaluations.\n• Support multi-discipline coordination by collaborating with mechanical, structural, civil engineers, and architects.\n• Communicate with clients, manufacturers, and contractors to address challenges and develop solutions.\n• Participate in project meetings and provide technical input.\n• Stay current with codes, standards, and emerging technologies.\n• Support project management tasks and contribute to proposals as needed.","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s or Associate’s degree in Electrical Engineering or related field.\n• EIT certification preferred; P.E. license or active pursuit a plus.\n• Minimum 5 years of electrical engineering experience within an A/E consulting firm (healthcare experience strongly preferred).\n• Proficiency with AutoCAD and Revit (required).\n• Familiarity with AGi32 (lighting) and SKM (power analysis).\n• Solid understanding of national, state, and local electrical codes.\n• Strong organizational, problem-solving, and communication skills.\n• Ability to handle multiple projects and meet deadlines.","whyConsider":"• Full electrical design ownership: power, lighting, telecom and generator, transformer and switchgear sizing.\n• Healthcare, higher education and institutional projects in Buffalo.\n• A clear step toward senior engineer and project lead.\n• Mentorship and ongoing training to keep your skills sharp as your career grows.\n• A collaborative, team-based culture where every voice counts.\n• Comprehensive benefits, including a 401(k), health insurance, PTO, life and disability insurance, and EIT and PE licensure support.","seoTitle":"Electrical Engineer | AGILE Position 1030","metaDescription":"Electrical Engineer in Buffalo, NY. Hybrid. Salary $85,000 to $125,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."}];
