\n• Provide technical solutions through close engagement with manufacturers and contractors.","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s or Associate’s degree in Electrical Engineering or Engineering Technology.\n• Professional Engineer (P.E.) license (NY or OH) strongly preferred.\n• Minimum 10 years of experience with an A/E consulting firm.\n• Proven expertise in power distribution, lighting, fire alarm, security, and telecommunications design.\n• Familiarity with AutoCAD, Revit, AGi32, SKM, and Arc-Flash evaluation.\n• Strong communication, organizational, and leadership skills.\n• Ability to manage multiple projects and deliver quality outcomes.","whyConsider":"• We will walk you through the role, privately and without pressure.\n• A leadership role for a senior engineer who is passionate about healthcare design.\n• A diverse mix of healthcare and commercial projects keeps the work interesting and your skills growing.\n• Exposure to high-performance, sustainable building design and decarbonization work.\n• A strong focus on professional development, with structured learning, mentorship and knowledge sharing.\n• A full benefits package: 401(k), health, life and disability insurance, paid time off, and EIT/PE licensure support."},{"id":"1030","responsibilities":"• Develop electrical designs for power distribution, lighting, telecommunications, fire alarm, and security systems.\n• Perform load calculations for generators, transformers, switchgear, panel boards, VFDs, feeders, and branch circuits.\n• Prepare electrical design drawings, specifications, and engineering reports.\n• Assist with building condition assessments and system evaluations.\n• Support multi-discipline coordination by collaborating with mechanical, structural, civil engineers, and architects.\n• Communicate with clients, manufacturers, and contractors to address challenges and develop solutions.\n• Participate in project meetings and provide technical input.\n• Stay current with codes, standards, and emerging technologies.\n• Support project management tasks and contribute to proposals as needed.","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s or Associate’s degree in Electrical Engineering or related field.\n• EIT certification preferred; P.E. license or active pursuit a plus.\n• Minimum 5 years of electrical engineering experience within an A/E consulting firm (healthcare experience strongly preferred).\n• Proficiency with AutoCAD and Revit (required).\n• Familiarity with AGi32 (lighting) and SKM (power analysis).\n• Solid understanding of national, state, and local electrical codes.\n• Strong organizational, problem-solving, and communication skills.\n• Ability to handle multiple projects and meet deadlines.","whyConsider":"• Full electrical design ownership: power, lighting, telecom and generator, transformer and switchgear sizing.\n• Healthcare, higher education and institutional projects in Buffalo.\n• A clear step toward senior engineer and project lead.\n• Mentorship and ongoing training to keep your skills sharp as your career grows.\n• A collaborative, team-based culture where every voice counts.\n• Comprehensive benefits, including a 401(k), health insurance, PTO, life and disability insurance, and EIT and PE licensure support.","seoTitle":"Electrical Engineer | AGILE Position 1030","metaDescription":"Electrical Engineer in Buffalo, NY. Hybrid. Salary $85,000 to $125,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."}];
