rds, and QA/QC protocols\n• Collaborate with multidisciplinary teams across electrical, plumbing, and fire protection\n• Mentor junior engineers and support staff development\n• Drive project schedules and maintain high-quality deliverables","qualifications":"• 10–15 years of HVAC engineering and project management experience\n• Bachelor’s Degree in Mechanical Engineering\n• Professional Engineer (PE) license preferred\n• Strong knowledge of building systems, HVAC design software, and NYC code compliance\n• Excellent leadership, communication, and problem-solving skills","whyConsider":"• Run HVAC projects from concept through CA, including mission critical, data center and healthcare work.\n• Own client communication, budgets and team coordination.\n• NYC code, sustainability and QA/QC leadership that sets you up for Associate.\n• Learn from senior engineers who make time to teach.\n• Team-based project delivery in a collaborative, supportive environment.\n• A full benefits package: 401(k), health, life and disability insurance, paid time off, and EIT/PE licensure support.","seoTitle":"Mechanical HVAC Project Manager | AGILE Position 1037","metaDescription":"Mechanical HVAC Project Manager in NYC, NY. Hybrid. Salary $135,000 to $165,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1038","responsibilities":"• Partner with department leadership to shape conceptual design and manage full project lifecycle\n• Serve as the primary point of contact for clients on assigned projects\n• Lead HVAC project teams, mentor junior engineers, and coordinate interdisciplinary tasks\n• Manage documentation accuracy and oversee timely delivery of design phases\n• Present and explain mechanical solutions clearly in internal and client meetings\n• Execute and monitor design changes, approvals, and proposals\n• Deliver multiple fit-out/renovation projects and/or large, mission-critical builds from concept to close-out","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s degree in Mechanical or Electrical Engineering\n• 8–14 years of mechanical engineering experience in building systems design\n• Mastery of HVAC design tools including Revit and AutoCAD\n• Strong project leadership, team coordination, and client-facing skills\n• Deep knowledge of mechanical codes, trade scopes, and deliverable standards\n• Proven track record managing complex multi-phase design and construction projects","whyConsider":"This is your opportunity to take the lead on high-impact projects while helping shape the future of a premier MEP firm. You’ll grow your leadership portfolio in a company that values innovation, technical excellence, and professional growth. Confidential virtual interviews are currently being scheduled.\nAvailable now.","seoTitle":"Associate, Mechanical | AGILE Position 1038","metaDescription":"Associate, Mechanical in NYC, NY. Hybrid Schedule. Salary $125,000 to $145,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1039","responsibilities":"• Lead the HVAC design and project delivery across a variety of sectors including education, healthcare, hospitality, and commercial facilities\n• Collaborate closely with firm Principals to develop project strategies, design solutions, and business development initiatives\n• Manage project schedules, budgets, and client relationships to ensure successful, on-time, and on-budget delivery\n• Mentor and develop junior staff to enhance team capabilities and support career growth\n• Ensure compliance with applicable codes, standards, and best practices\n• Participate in design reviews, quality control, and coordination with other disciplines","qualifications":"• Minimum of 8 years HVAC engineering experience with strong project management exposure\n• Professional Engineering (PE) license preferred\n• Proven leadership skills with experience managing teams and mentoring staff\n• Excellent communication, organizational, and client-facing skills\n• Ability to manage multiple priorities and projects effectively\n• Experience with relevant design software and tools","whyConsider":"• Lead HVAC design and delivery working directly with firm principals.\n• Choose White Plains or NYC as your home office.\n• Healthcare, campus and hospitality work with real budget and client ownership.\n• Training, mentoring and knowledge sharing are part of how the firm works.\n• Sustainable, energy-efficient design is part of the work, not an afterthought.\n• Comprehensive benefits, including a 401(k), health insurance, PTO, life and disability insurance, and EIT and PE licensure support.","seoTitle":"Senior HVAC Engineer / Project Manager | AGILE Position 1039","metaDescription":"Senior HVAC Engineer / Project Manager in White Plains, NY; NYC, NY. Hybrid. Salary $120,000 to $170,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1040","seoTitle":"Associate Mechanical Engineer – Data Centers (HVAC) – New York, NY | AGILE Position 1040","metaDescription":"Associate Mechanical Engineer (Data Centers/HVAC) in New York, NY. Remote role. 10+ years of MEP mechanical engineering experience in mission-critical HVAC design. Salary $125,000 to $150,000+. Review confidential career details from AGILE.","responsibilities":"• Lead HVAC design and engineering for greenfield, retrofit, and live upgrade data center projects\n• Define and coordinate mechanical system requirements with plumbing, fire protection, electrical, and controls teams\n• Develop engineering standards and scalable design solutions tailored to 24/7 mission critical facilities\n• Interface with clients, architects, and commissioning teams to align technical delivery with project goals\n• Optimize system performance in collaboration with energy modeling teams, ensuring compliance with ASHRAE 90.1/90.4 and TC 9.9 standards\n• Design and review systems including chillers, cooling towers, air handlers, heat pumps, generator ventilation, and fuel oil systems\n• Participate in QA/QC, peer reviews, and value engineering exercises to elevate project quality\n• Represent the firm at national conferences, industry panels, and technical workshops\n• Travel to client sites across the U.S. as needed for design coordination and field verification","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s Degree in Mechanical Engineering (or equivalent technical degree)\n• 10+ years of experience in HVAC design, including work on mission critical or data center projects\n• Proficient in Revit and BIM coordination workflows\n• Strong knowledge of HVAC system design including chilled water, CRAC/CRAH, economizers, and standby generation support systems\n• Familiarity with energy modeling and building controls systems\n• PE license strongly preferred\n• Excellent communication and client-facing project management skills\n• Ability to lead cross-functional design teams and mentor junior staff","whyConsider":"Available now."}];
