btain PE within 1–2 years considered\n• Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment\n• Willingness and ability to travel as needed","whyConsider":"• Engineer and PM in one: complex healthcare and commercial mechanical design plus project leadership.\n• Own scope, reports, design development and field implementation.\n• A fast-track path to Senior PM for a 4–7 year engineer.\n• A strong focus on professional development, with structured learning, mentorship and knowledge sharing.\n• A collaborative culture that values your ideas, not just your output.\n• A full benefits package: 401(k), health, life and disability insurance, paid time off, and EIT/PE licensure support."},{"id":"1054","responsibilities":"• Lead mechanical project design activities with minimal supervision.\n• Prepare project plans, specifications, and cost estimates.\n• Provide direction to Designers and CAD Operators, reviewing drawings and ensuring accuracy.\n• Establish design concepts, criteria, and scope while coordinating across trades, architects, and clients.\n• Perform engineering calculations, equipment selection, and system sizing.\n• Review shop drawings and recommend improvements to engineering standards.\n• Collaborate with Principals, Associates, and Senior Engineers to clarify scope and deliverables.","qualifications":"• Bachelor of Science in Mechanical Engineering or equivalent.\n• Professional Engineer (P.E.) license preferred; E.I.T. working toward licensure considered.\n• Minimum 2 years’ experience with responsibility for project design.\n• Strong knowledge of mechanical systems design and construction coordination.\n• Ability to supervise and mentor junior team members.","whyConsider":"• Lead mechanical design with minimal supervision, directing designers and CAD operators.\n• Prepare plans, specifications and cost estimates: the full engineer toolkit.\n• Buffalo-based with a clear step to Senior Mechanical Engineer.\n• Diverse project types across co