stitutional projects, all under one roof.\n• Benefits include a 401(k), health insurance, paid time off, life and disability insurance, and EIT and PE licensure support.","seoTitle":"Senior Mechanical Engineer | AGILE Position 1055","metaDescription":"Senior Mechanical Engineer in Buffalo, NY. Hybrid. Salary $88,000 to $120,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1056","responsibilities":"• Lead design of building HVAC systems and district energy systems.\n• Conduct field investigations to document existing conditions.\n• Perform system selection and calculations for design purposes.\n• Work with junior engineers to review drawings and project documentation.\n• Engage directly with clients on design options, cost-benefit analyses, and decision-making.\n• Ensure compliance with codes, standards, and utility requirements.","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s degree in Mechanical Engineering preferred.\n• 8–10 years of relevant experience in HVAC and hydronic system design.\n• Preferred: experience designing geothermal or district energy systems.\n• Proficiency with Revit or AutoCAD.\n• New York State P.E. license a plus.\n• Excellent verbal and written communication skills.","whyConsider":"• We are currently scheduling confidential interviews for this position.\n• If you’re a Mechanical Engineer ready to lead innovative projects and grow your career, we’d like to connect.\n• A diverse mix of commercial and energy and utilities projects keeps the work interesting and your skills growing.\n• Continuous learning is built in: mentorship, in-house training and knowledge sharing across teams.\n• A collaborative, team-based culture where every voice counts.\n• Benefits: 401(k), health insurance, paid time off, life and disability coverage, and support for EIT and PE licensure.","seoTitle":"Mechanical Engineer – Energy Infrastructure (Mid-Level) | AGILE Position 1056","metaDescription":"Mechanical Engineer – Energy Infrastructure (Mid-Level) in Buffalo, NY. Hy