l Project Engineer in Rochester, NY. Hybrid role. 2+ years of MEP mechanical engineering and HVAC project delivery experience. Salary $73,000 to $88,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE.","responsibilities":"• Independently evaluate, select, and apply standard engineering techniques and procedures.\n• Work with Principals, Associates, and Senior Engineers to clarify project scope and deliverables.\n• Supervise and guide Designers and CAD Operators on project tasks.\n• Prepare project plans, specifications, and cost estimates.\n• Establish project design concepts, criteria, and scope.\n• Perform engineering computations, equipment selection, and system sizing.\n• Coordinate with trades, architects, and clients.\n• Review shop drawings and recommend improvements to firm standards.\n• Ensure accuracy of designs, drawings, and specifications.\n• Provide leadership and oversight throughout all phases of project work.","qualifications":"• Bachelor of Science in Mechanical Engineering or equivalent.\n• Professional Engineer (P.E.) license preferred; E.I.T. working toward licensure considered.\n• Minimum 2 years’ experience with responsibility for project design.\n• Strong technical knowledge of mechanical systems and construction coordination.\n• Ability to supervise, mentor, and coordinate design teams.","whyConsider":"• Reach out to us; first conversations are always confidential.\n• If you’re a Mechanical Project Engineer seeking to advance your career with a respected firm, we’d be glad to connect with you.\n• Broaden your portfolio across healthcare, higher education, commercial, and institutional projects.\n• Learn from senior engineers who make time to teach.\n• Team-based project delivery in a collaborative, supportive environment.\n• Comprehensive benefits, including a 401(k), health insurance, PTO, life and disability insurance, and EIT and PE licensure support."},{"id":"1059","responsibilities":"• Lead and oversee mechanical engineering projects th