rchitects, engineers, contractors, and clients to meet project schedules and goals.","qualifications":"\u2022 Bachelor\u2019s degree in Electrical Engineering (PE preferred).\n\u2022 4+ years of professional electrical design experience, with at least 2 years in a senior-level role.\n\u2022 Strong knowledge of NEC, NYC codes, and industry standards.\n\u2022 Proficiency in AutoCAD and Revit.\n\u2022 Strong communication and organizational skills; proven ability to manage deadlines.\n\u2022 Client-facing presence with the ability to represent the firm in meetings.","whyConsider":"• This is a chance to join an award-winning team where you’ll make a visible impact on high-profile NYC projects.\n• You will work on complex, high-performance facilities while mentoring future engineers and advancing your own career in a firm known for stability, growth, and excellence.\n• Work spans mission critical, healthcare, higher education, and commercial, so no two projects feel the same.\n• A team culture built on respect and shared credit.\n• Benefits include a 401(k), health insurance, paid time off, life and disability insurance, and EIT and PE licensure support.","seoTitle":"Senior Electrical Designer | AGILE Position 1090","metaDescription":"Senior Electrical Designer in NYC, NY. Hybrid. Salary $110,000 to $125,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."}];
