, and support for EIT and PE licensure.","seoTitle":"Senior HVAC Engineer | AGILE Position 1094","metaDescription":"Senior HVAC Engineer in NYC, NY. Hybrid. Salary $140,000 to $170,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1095","responsibilities":"• Develop HVAC and mechanical system designs, layouts, and schematics.\n• Perform load calculations, energy modeling, and equipment selections.\n• Review shop drawings, oversee construction documents, and conduct site visits.\n• Coordinate across disciplines to ensure integrated project delivery.\n• Act as Job Captain—owning quality control, schedules, and team deliverables.\n• Mentor and train junior staff.","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s degree in Mechanical Engineering; PE license preferred.\n• 6+ years of mechanical/HVAC design experience.\n• Proficiency in AutoCAD, Revit, and Microsoft Office.\n• Knowledge of codes, standards, and construction practices.\n• Strong communication, problem-solving, and organizational skills.","whyConsider":"• Job Captain responsibility: QC, schedule and deliverables are yours.\n• The firm is actively expanding in Florida, with a strong pipeline of awarded projects.\n• Energy modeling and full HVAC design, not drafting support.\n• Studio teams of up to 15 with the backing of a firm licensed across 35+ states.\n• Extras like free financial planning and on-site fitness and wellness programs.\n• Long careers are the norm here, with typical tenure of over ten years.\n• Leadership invests in your progression, with a mapped route to your next role.\n• Expect variety: commercial, energy and utilities, and media and broadcast assignments, often in the same year.\n• Benefits include a retirement plan, medical, dental and vision, paid time off, and EIT and PE licensure support.","seoTitle":"Senior Mechanical Designer – Job Captain | AGILE Position 1095","metaDescription":"Senior Mechanical Designer – Job Captain in Hollywood, FL. Hybrid. Salary $110,000 to $145,000. Review confi