outs, and equipment selection.\n• Develop schematics, specifications, and construction documents using AutoCAD and Revit.\n• Support construction administration, including shop drawing reviews, RFIs, and field observations.\n• Ensure compliance with ASHRAE, Florida Building Codes, and energy standards.\n• Mentor junior staff and assist in Job Captain responsibilities.\n• Collaborate with architects, engineers, contractors, and clients to achieve project goals.","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s degree in Mechanical Engineering (PE license preferred).\n• 4+ years of progressive mechanical design experience; HVAC focus required.\n• Strong proficiency in AutoCAD and Revit.\n• In-depth knowledge of codes, standards, and building systems design.\n• Excellent communication, time management, and organizational skills.\n• Ability to manage multiple projects in a fast-paced environment.","whyConsider":"• Growing South Florida office of a firm with projects in 30+ states.\n• Healthcare, higher-ed and mission critical work from a strong awarded-project pipeline.\n• A clear step toward Job Captain responsibility.\n• Mentoring junior staff is built into the role.\n• Low turnover and long tenure: many people build their whole career here.\n• Structured in-house training, plus a career development plan tailored to you.\n• Benefits: retirement plan, medical, dental and vision coverage, paid time off, and EIT and PE licensure support.","seoTitle":"Senior Mechanical Designer – Healthcare & Institutional | AGILE Position 1097","metaDescription":"Senior Mechanical Designer – Healthcare & Institutional in Hollywood, FL. Hybrid. Salary $110,000 to $135,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1098","seoTitle":"Mechanical Project Manager – HVAC – Wall Township, NJ | AGILE Position 1098","metaDescription":"Project Manager, Mechanical (HVAC), in Wall Township, NJ. On-site role. 10+ years of MEP mechanical engineering experience leading complex HVAC project delivery. Salary $115,000 to $180,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE.","responsibilities":"• Lead and manage HVAC design for a wide range of building types\n• Oversee design, coordination & execution of mechanical systems to code/client standards\n• Manage budgets, schedules, resources, and project delivery\n• Provide technical expertise in HVAC design (load calcs, system sizing, equipment selection, controls, energy efficiency)\n• Prepare drawings, specifications, and technical reports\n• Serve as the primary client contact throughout project lifecycle\n• Coordinate designs with other disciplines to ensure seamless integration\n• Conduct site visits for field verification, administration, and commissioning support\n• Mentor and train junior engineers; provide leadership and oversight\n• Contribute to proposals, bids, and business development efforts","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s or Master’s in Mechanical Engineering (required)\n• PE License in NJ (favored); LEED or sustainability certifications a plus\n• 10+ years HVAC design experience in consulting engineering, with proven project management skills\n• Advanced proficiency with HVAC design software (Trane Trace, Carrier HAP, EnergyPlus) and AutoCAD/Revit\n• Familiarity with green building standards (LEED, WELL, BREEAM)\n• Strong leadership, communication, and client management abilities\n• PMP certification a plus","whyConsider":"• Project Manager authority with technical leadership in HVAC.\n• An ENR Top 500 firm every year, plus other national industry rankings.\n• MEP, structural, geotechnical and land development under one roof.\n• Multiple Project of the Year awards.\n• On-site in Wall Township. Reach out to us; first conversations are always confidential.\n• Promotion criteria are clear from the start, so you can plan your career with confidence.\n• A busy, well-booked project calendar that supports long-term growth.\n• Build a well-rounded résumé across commercial, institutional, residential, and industrial work.\n• Comprehensive benefits, including a 401(k), health insurance, PTO, life and disability insurance, and EIT and PE licensure support."},{"id":"1099","seoTitle":"Mechanical Engineer (HVAC) – Wall Township, NJ | AGILE Position 1099","metaDescription":"Mechanical Engineer (HVAC) in Wall Township, NJ. On-site role. 3 to 10 years of MEP mechanical engineering experience in HVAC systems design. Salary $90,000 to $140,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE.","responsibilities":"• Design HVAC systems including load calculations, equipment selection, ductwork/piping layouts & controls\n• Prepare detailed drawings, specifications & construction documents using AutoCAD and Revit\n• Perform energy modeling, life-cycle cost analysis & code compliance reviews\n• Coordinate HVAC designs with architectural, structural, electrical, and plumbing disciplines\n• Conduct site visits for investigations, construction admin & commissioning support\n• Review submittals, respond to RFIs & resolve construction issues\n• Collaborate with clients, team members, and consultants to meet project goals\n• Support proposal preparation and client presentations","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s degree in Mechanical Engineering or related field\n• EIT or PE in NJ/NY (highly preferred)\n• 3–10 years of HVAC design experience in consulting engineering\n• Proficiency with HVAC software (Carrier HAP, Trane Trace, or similar)\n• Experience with AutoCAD and Revit (required)\n• Familiarity with ASHRAE standards, building and energy codes\n• Strong written, verbal, and coordination skills","whyConsider":"• Energy modeling and life-cycle cost analysis, not just layouts.\n• An ENR Top 500 firm every year, named to a Best Places to Work list.\n• Mentorship and a firm culture of growing leaders internally.\n• Multiple East Coast offices and multi-discipline project teams.\n• On-site in Wall Township. Talk with us first; your search stays private.\n• A clear, mapped-out career path, so you know what advancement looks like and what it takes to get there.\n• A strong project pipeline means steady, meaningful work and the stability to build a long-term career.\n• Diverse project types across healthcare, commercial, and energy and utilities work, so your experience keeps broadening.\n• Benefits include a 401(k), health insurance, paid time off, life and disability insurance, and EIT and PE licensure support."},{"id":"1100","responsibilities":"• Design HVAC systems: load calculations, equipment selection, duct/piping layout & controls\n• Prepare drawings, specifications & construction documents in AutoCAD/Revit\n• Perform energy modeling, cost analyses, and code compliance reviews\n• Coordinate HVAC designs with other disciplines (architectural, structural, MEP)\n• Conduct site visits for investigations, construction admin & commissioning\n• Review submittals, respond to RFIs & assist with issue resolution\n• Support proposals & participate in client meetings as appropriate","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s degree in Mechanical Engineering (required)\n• EIT or PE in NJ/NY (highly preferred)\n• 3–10 years of HVAC design experience in consulting engineering\n• Proficiency with HVAC design software (Carrier HAP, Trane Trace, etc.)\n• Experience with AutoCAD and Revit (required)\n• Knowledge of ASHRAE standards, building/energy codes\n• Strong written, verbal, and project coordination skills","whyConsider":"AGILE’s Client offers competitive pay, hybrid flexibility, and comprehensive benefits including medical/dental/vision, 401k with match, PTO, tuition reimbursement, and professional development. With a proven reputation for innovation and technical excellence, this is an opportunity to contribute to impactful projects while advancing your career in a respected firm. If you’re a mechanical engineer seeking to deepen your HVAC expertise and contribute to high-profile projects, we encourage you to apply in 2026.\nAvailable now.","seoTitle":"Mechanical Engineer (HVAC) | AGILE Position 1100"}];
