th technical documentation, calculations, and project coordination\n• Support communication with clients, architects, and consultants\n• Contribute to high-quality engineering deliverables and project execution","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s Degree in Electrical Engineering preferred\n• 3–7 years of Building Systems / MEP Consulting experience\n• Background with lighting, power, and special systems design\n• Exposure to low voltage, fire alarm, and security systems\n• Experience with short circuit, protective device, and arc flash analysis studies is a plus\n• FE / EIT Certification preferred\n• PE Licensure is a plus\n• Strong communication and coordination abilities","whyConsider":"• Architects, engineers and interior designers under one roof, so coordination is face to face.\n• Portfolio highlights: corporate headquarters, a flagship department store, a colocation data center, a medical college and historic landmark work.\n• Principals are working members of every project team.\n• Offices in Clarks Summit and Manhattan.\n• Benefits: 401(k), health insurance, paid time off, life and disability coverage, and support for EIT and PE licensure.","seoTitle":"Electrical Designer / Engineer | AGILE Position 1146","metaDescription":"Electrical Designer / Engineer in Clarks Summit, PA. Hybrid. Salary $78,000 to $95,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1147","responsibilities":"• Design and analysis of HVAC systems including air distribution systems, hydronic systems, mechanical equipment selection, and controls concepts\n• Support Energy Modeling and Life Cycle Cost Analysis efforts\n• Design and coordinate plumbing systems and fire protection systems\n• Coordinate across engineering disciplines and project stakeholders\n• Participate in projects from design through construction administration\n• Assist with technical documentation, calculations, and project coordination\n• Support communication with clients, architects, and consultants\n• Contribute to high-quality engineering deliverables and project execution","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s Degree in Mechanical Engineering preferred\n• 3–7 years of Building Systems / MEP Consulting experience\n• Background with HVAC, plumbing, and/or fire protection system design\n• Experience with air distribution systems, hydronic systems, and equipment selection\n• FE / EIT Certification preferred\n• Professional Engineering licensure is a plus\n• Strong communication and coordination abilities","whyConsider":"• Full mechanical scope, including energy modeling and LCCA.\n• Corporate headquarters, data center, medical college and historic landmark work in the portfolio.\n• In-house architects mean real collaboration, not markups across firms.\n• Principals stay hands-on on every project.\n• A full benefits package: 401(k), health, life and disability insurance, paid time off, and EIT/PE licensure support.","seoTitle":"Mechanical Designer / Engineer | AGILE Position 1147","metaDescription":"Mechanical Designer / Engineer in Clarks Summit, PA. Hybrid. Salary $78,000 to $95,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1148","responsibilities":"• Coordinate modeling conflicts across Mechanical, Electrical, and Plumbing disciplines\n• Support and enhance BIM processes, standards, and design technology workflows\n• Develop and maintain scripts to automate repetitive modeling and documentation tasks\n• Implement and manage BIM standards and workflows across projects\n• Ensure models meet quality standards and support project objectives\n• Serve as a technical resource for Revit and BIM automation tools\n• Support project teams from design concept through construction documentation\n• Provide guidance and training related to BIM processes and Revit usage\n• Stay current with emerging BIM and design technologies","qualifications":"• Relevant CAD, Revit, and BIM experience within MEP / Building Systems projects\n• Background with Mechanical, Electrical, and Plumbin