 systems\n• Experience with short circuit, protective device, and arc flash analysis studies is a plus\n• Professional Engineering licensure preferred\n• Strong communication, coordination, and leadership abilities","whyConsider":"• Engineer and Project Manager in one senior role.\n• Corporate headquarters, data center, flagship retail and landmark projects in the portfolio.\n• Offices in Clarks Summit and Manhattan, with principals on every team.\n• Communication, trust and teamwork are the firm's stated hallmarks.\n• Benefits include a 401(k), health insurance, paid time off, life and disability insurance, and EIT and PE licensure support.","seoTitle":"Senior Electrical Engineer / Project Manager | AGILE Position 1149","metaDescription":"Senior Electrical Engineer / Project Manager in Clarks Summit, PA. Hybrid. Salary $105,000 to $145,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1150","responsibilities":"• Design and analysis of HVAC systems including air distribution systems, hydronic systems, mechanical equipment selection, and controls concepts\n• Support Energy Modeling and Life Cycle Cost Analysis efforts\n• Design and coordinate plumbing systems and fire protection systems\n• Coordinate across engineering disciplines and project stakeholders\n• Oversee projects from design through construction administration\n• Mentor and support junior engineering staff\n• Assist with technical documentation, calculations, and project coordination\n• Support communication with clients, architects, and consultants\n• Contribute to high-quality engineering deliverables and project execution\n• Support project management and technical leadership efforts","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s Degree in Mechanical Engineering preferred\n• 8+ years of Building Systems / MEP Consulting experience\n• Background with HVAC, plumbing, and/or fire protection system design\n• Experience with air distribution systems, hydronic systems, and equipment selection\n• Professional Engineering licensure preferred\n• Strong communication, coordination, and leadership abilities","whyConsider":"• Senior engineer and PM authority across the full mechanical scope.\n• In-house architects and interior designers on every project.\n• Corporate, data center, medical college and landmark work in the portfolio.\n• Principals are working members of the team.\n• Benefits: 401(k), health insurance, paid time off, life and disability coverage, and support for EIT and PE licensure.","seoTitle":"Senior Mechanical Engineer / Project Manager | AGILE Position 1150","metaDescription":"Senior Mechanical Engineer / Project Manager in Clarks Summit, PA. Hybrid. Salary $105,000 to $145,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1151","responsibilities":"• Lead electrical systems design across all project phases\n• Support power distribution, lighting controls, life safety, and specialty systems design\n• Develop electrical room layouts, distribution strategies, and equipment selections\n• Write electrical specifications and sequences of operation\n• Conduct field surveys, due diligence reports, and construction administration activities\n• Review RFIs, submittals, and shop drawings\n• Coordinate across multidisciplinary project teams and stakeholders\n• Mentor junior engineering and design staff\n• Support QA/QC efforts and technical leadership initiatives\n• Participate in client meetings, walkthroughs, and project coordination sessions","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s Degree in Electrical Engineering preferred\n• 8+ years of Building Systems / MEP Consulting experience\n• Strong background with lighting, power distribution, and electrical systems coordination\n• Experience with load calculations, voltage drop analysis, and panel scheduling\n• Knowledge of NEC, NFPA, NYC Electrical Code, and related standards\n• Experience supporting multidisciplinary project coordination\n• Professional Engineering licensure preferred\n• Strong communication, coordination, and leadership abilities","whyConsider":"• Three Lead openings on one team: a direct sign of a strong awarded-project pipeline.\n• You write the specs and sequences of operation, not just the drawings.\n• Due diligence, field survey and CA experience on complex NYC buildings.\n• Studio teams of up to 15 with the resources of a 300+ person firm.\n• Lead sooner, and keep your options open across specialties.\n• Advancement is planned, not left to chance: you'll know the milestones for your next title.\n• Diverse project types across healthcare, commercial, and institutional work, so your experience keeps broadening.\n• Perks include complimentary financial planning and wellness programs, with on-site fitness.\n• Benefits include a retirement plan, medical, dental and vision, paid time off, and EIT and PE licensure support.","seoTitle":"Lead Electrical Designer | AGILE Position 1151","metaDescription":"Lead Electrical Designer in NYC, NY. Hybrid. Salary $135,000 . to $175,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1152","responsibilities":"• Design electrical systems independently across multiple project phases\n• Support lighting, power distribution, life safety, and specialty systems design\n• Perform electrical load calculations, voltage drop analysis, and panel scheduling\n• Participate in advanced electrical room layouts and system coordination\n• Generate electrical specifications and technical documentation\n• Conduct field surveys, shop drawing reviews, and construction administration activities\n• Coordinate across multidisciplinary project teams and stakeholders\n• Participate in project meetings and client coordination discussions\n• Mentor junior engineering and design staff\n• Support QA/QC initiatives and documentation quality efforts","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s Degree in Electrical Engineering preferred\n• 4+ years of Building Systems / MEP Consulting experience\n• Strong background with lighting, power distribution, and electrical systems coordination\n• Experience with AutoCAD, Revit, and electrical design software\n• Knowledge of NEC, NFPA, energy codes, and related standards\n• Experience with load calculations, voltage drop analysis, and electrical system layouts\n• FE Certification or pursuit of PE licensure is a plus\n• Strong communication, coordination, and leadership abilities","whyConsider":"• Two openings on a team with a strong pipeline of awarded projects.\n• Independent design responsibility across multiple project phases.\n• Exposure to advanced electrical room layout and system coordination.\n• A clear track toward Lead Electrical Designer.\n• A team that stays together, with tenure measured in decades, not years.\n• The firm maps out each engineer's path to promotion, so growth is visible and measurable.\n• Variety you won't get everywhere: healthcare, commercial, institutional, and energy and utilities projects, all under one roof.\n• Complimentary financial planning, plus on-site fitness and wellness programs.\n• Benefits: retirement plan, medical, dental and vision coverage, paid time off, and EIT and PE licensure support.","seoTitle":"Senior Electrical Designer | AGILE Position 1152","metaDescription":"Senior Electrical Designer in NYC, NY. Hybrid. Salary $105,000 to $140,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."}];
