-export default [{"id":"1159","responsibilities":"• Design building electrical systems including power distribution, lighting, emergency power, fire alarm, and low voltage systems\n• Prepare electrical engineering plans, specifications, calculations, and construction documentation\n• Utilize AutoCAD and Revit to produce engineering plans and system layouts\n• Coordinate electrical systems with internal multi discipline engineering teams\n• Review shop drawings, RFIs, and construction documentation\n• Perform field surveys and evaluations of existing facilities\n• Support projects throughout NY, NJ, and PA markets\n• Participate in client coordination meetings and project discussions","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s Degree in Electrical Engineering from an ABET accredited program\n• 5+ to 10 years of Building Systems Electrical Engineering experience\n• Strong proficiency utilizing AutoCAD and Revit\n• Experience designing commercial, healthcare, educational, industrial, or mission critical facilities\n• Strong knowledge of power distribution, lighting, emergency power, and fire alarm systems\n• Familiarity with applicable electrical codes and standards\n• Strong communication and organizational abilities\n• Ability to work independently and collaboratively within team environments\nPreferred Qualifications:\n• Professional Engineer registration preferred\n• Experience supporting multi discipline consulting projects\nBenefits:\n• Competitive compensation package\n• Performance bonuses\n• 401(k)\n• Health, Dental, Vision, and Life Insurance\n• Flexible Spending Account and Health Savings Account\n• Paid Vacation, Sick Time, and Holidays\n• Continuing education and PE registration incentives\n• Hybrid schedule flexibility\n• Long term advancement opportunities","whyConsider":"This is an excellent opportunity to join a highly established consulting environment supporting a diverse portfolio of commercial, healthcare, educational, industrial, and mission critical projects throughout the Northeast. Engineers here gain exposure to collaborative project teams, strong technical mentorship, hybrid flexibility, and long term professional growth opportunities within a respected organization.\nAvailable now.","seoTitle":"Electrical Engineer | AGILE Position 1159","metaDescription":"Electrical Engineer in NYC, NY. Hybrid Schedule. Salary $115,000 to $150,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1160","responsibilities":"• Design building structures utilizing structural steel, reinforced concrete, reinforced masonry, and wood construction\n• Utilize Bentley Systems, Enercalc, and PCA engineering software to design structural systems\n• Produce engineering plans and documentation utilizing AutoCAD and Revit\n• Draft foundation plans, framing plans, structural details, and construction sections\n• Review shop drawings and construction documentation\n• Perform surveys and evaluations of existing buildings\n• Coordinate closely with internal multi discipline engineering teams\n• Support projects throughout PA, NY, and NJ markets","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s Degree in Engineering from an ABET accredited program\n• 5 to 10 years of Structural Engineering experience\n• Strong proficiency utilizing Bentley Systems, Enercalc, and PCA engineering software\n• Proficiency utilizing AutoCAD and Revit\n• Experience designing buildings up to 5 stories in height utilizing structural steel, reinforced concrete, reinforced masonry, and wood systems\n• Strong communication and organizational abilities\n• Ability to work independently and collaboratively within team environments\n• Experience supporting multi discipline project teams\n• Professional Engineer registration preferred","whyConsider":"• Structural design across four materials and six markets.\n• Architects in the same office, so you design with them, not after them.\n• Data center, corporate headquarters and landmark work in the portfolio.\n• Principals stay hands-on on every project.\n• A full benefits package: 401(k), health, life and disability insurance, paid time off, and EIT/PE licensure support.","seoTitle":"Structural Engineer | AGILE Position 1160","metaDescription":"Structural Engineer in Clarks Summit, PA. Hybrid. Salary $90,000 to $120,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1161","responsibilities":"• Manage multiple civil engineering projects from planning through construction.\n• Lead multidisciplinary engineering teams while coordinating with Structural, Geotechnical, Environmental, Architectural, and MEP disciplines.\n• Prepare and manage project scopes, budgets, schedules, and technical quality control.\n• Develop engineering calculations, reports, construction drawings, and technical specifications.\n• Serve as the primary client contact throughout project execution.\n• Lead project meetings, coordinate with contractors, and perform field visits as needed.\n• Support proposal preparation, project pursuits, and business development activities.\n• Mentor and oversee junior and mid-level engineering staff.","qualifications":"• Bachelor's degree in Civil Engineering required; Master's degree preferred.\n• Active New York Professional Engineer (P.E.) license favored.\n• 10 to 15 years of civil engineering design and project management experience.\n• Extensive experience delivering projects for agencies such as NYSDOT, NYCDDC, NYCEDC, NYCDOT, NYCDEP, and NYCDPR.\n• Strong understanding of AASHTO, MUTCD, stormwater design, SWPPP, MS4/USWR requirements, and applicable NYC Building Codes.\n• Experience preparing project scopes, budgets, schedules, and engineering proposals.\n• Working knowledge of permitting processes and agency design standards.\n• Proficiency with AutoCAD, MicroStation, and/or Civil 3D.\n• Experience leading multidisciplinary engineering teams on complex public infrastructure projects.\n• Strong leadership, communication, organizational, and client relationship skills.\n• Clean driving record required.\nPreferred Experience:\n• Design-Build project delivery.\n• Additional Professional Engineer licenses in other states.\n• NCEES Record.\n• Experience supporting both public and private sector infrastructure projects.","whyConsider":"• Program-scale public infrastructure: transportation, resilience and stormwater work in the New York market.\n• Civil engineering plus a full MEP consulting practice in-house, for complete project teams.\n• A growing national design-build practice adds alternative-delivery opportunities.\n• All disciplines in-house, so you lead the whole team, not a patchwork of subconsultants.\n• Family-owned for decades: long-term thinking and stable leadership.\n• A defined promotion path, with regular conversations about where you're headed next.\n• Steady client demand keeps the project pipeline strong.\n• 401(k) match, tuition reimbursement and leadership development programs.\n• Health insurance, paid time off, and EIT and PE licensure support.","seoTitle":"Senior Civil Project Manager | AGILE Position 1161","metaDescription":"Senior Civil Project Manager in NYC, NY. Hybrid. Salary $170,000 to $230,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1162","responsibilities":"• Prepare and review highway and roadway design plans, engineering estimates, technical specifications, and construction details.\n• Develop conceptual and final engineering documents including horizontal and vertical roadway alignments.\n• Design roadway geometry, site grading, drainage systems, utilities, construction staging, traffic signals, pavement markings, and signage.\n• Assist Project Managers with day-to-day project coordination and technical execution.\n• Provide technical guidance and mentorship to junior engineers and technical staff.\n• Coordinate with multidisciplinary project teams to deliver high-quality engineering solutions.\n• Ensure design compliance with applicable agency standards and project requirements.","qualifications":"• Bachelor's degree in Civil Engineering required; Master's degree in Civil or Transportation Engineering preferred.\n• Active New York Professional Engineer (P.E.) license favored.\n• 8 to 12 years of highway, roadway, and transportation engineering experience.\n• Strong experience designing projects for agencies such as NYSDOT, NYCDOT, NYCDDC, NYCT, TBTA, or similar public agencies.\n• Thorough understanding of highway engineering, roadway design, grading, drainage, utility coordination, stormwater management, and Maintenance & Protection of Traffic (MPT).\n• Working knowledge of FHWA MUTCD, AASHTO, New York State DOT, and New York City DOT design standards.\n• Proficiency with MicroStation and OpenRoads required.\n• Experience with AutoCAD and Civil 3D preferred.\n• Strong organizational, communication, and technical problem-solving skills.\n• Clean driving record required.\nPreferred Experience:\n• Transportation corridor improvements.\n• Municipal roadway reconstruction.\n• Public infrastructure design.\n• Stormwater management and watershed analysis.\n• Multidisciplinary project coordination.","whyConsider":"• Real corridor work: alignments, geometry, drainage and staging, not just plan production.\n• Civil and MEP teams under one roof, so projects are delivered end to end.\n• A national transportation practice with design-build pursuits nationwide.\n• Mentorship by senior engineers and a clear track to Project Manager.\n• Family-owned for decades, with stable leadership.\n• Clear expectations for advancement, laid out early and revisited as you grow.\n• A strong backlog, so you can focus on great work rather than the next assignment.\n• A diverse mix of transportation and government projects keeps the work interesting and your skills growing.\n• Tuition reimbursement, training programs and 401(k) with company match.\n• Health coverage, paid time off and support for EIT and PE licensure.","seoTitle":"Senior Highway/Civil Engineer | AGILE Position 1162","metaDescription":"Senior Highway/Civil Engineer in NYC, NY. Hybrid. Salary $142,000 to $185,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."}];
