-export default [{"id":"1168","responsibilities":"• Manage water and wastewater infrastructure projects from planning through construction support.\n• Lead the planning, design, and construction oversight of water distribution, wastewater collection, conveyance, and treatment facilities.\n• Prepare and review engineering reports, calculations, technical specifications, bid documents, and construction deliverables.\n• Manage project scopes, budgets, schedules, quality control, and overall client satisfaction.\n• Coordinate multidisciplinary engineering teams, subconsultants, contractors, and public agencies.\n• Develop proposals, statements of qualifications (SOQs), project scopes, fee estimates, and project execution plans.\n• Mentor junior engineers while supporting continued growth of the Water Resources practice.\n• Assist with business development initiatives and expansion of public and industrial sector client relationships.","qualifications":"• Bachelor's degree in Civil Engineering or Environmental Engineering required.\n• Active Colorado Professional Engineer (P.E.) license required or the ability to obtain.\n• Master's degree in Engineering preferred.\n• 8+ years of experience in water and wastewater engineering.\n• Strong background in planning, design, and construction oversight of water and wastewater infrastructure projects.\n• Experience managing project budgets, schedules, quality, and client relationships.\n• Proven ability to lead multidisciplinary engineering teams and deliver successful projects.\n• Strong written, verbal, organizational, and project management skills.\n• Demonstrated commitment to technical excellence and responsive client service.\nPreferred Experience:\n• Water treatment facilities.\n• Wastewater treatment facilities.\n• Water transmission and distribution systems.\n• Wastewater collection and conveyance systems.\n• Public agency and industrial water infrastructure projects.\n• Business development and client relationship management.","whyConsider":"Join a top-rated ENR engineering consulting firm and help deliver essential water and wastewater infrastructure projects that support growing communities throughout Colorado. You'll work alongside highly respected engineering professionals on planning, design, and construction projects involving water treatment, wastewater treatment, conveyance systems, and critical public infrastructure. This opportunity offers a competitive compensation package, performance bonuses, relocation assistance, a hybrid work schedule, outstanding career development, and the opportunity to build lasting relationships with public and industrial sector clients while advancing your leadership career.\nAvailable now.","seoTitle":"Water / Wastewater Project Manager | AGILE Position 1168","metaDescription":"Water / Wastewater Project Manager in Denver, CO. Hybrid Schedule. Salary $125,000 to $145,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1169","responsibilities":"• Serve as Project Engineer on municipal water and wastewater infrastructure projects from planning through construction.\n• Design and support large-diameter pipelines, pump stations, lift stations, water treatment facilities, and wastewater treatment facilities.\n• Perform hydraulic calculations, system modeling, facility sizing, and engineering analyses.\n• Prepare engineering reports, bid documents, construction drawings, specifications, and technical deliverables.\n• Coordinate with project managers, engineers, subconsultants, contractors, and public agency clients.\n• Assist with permitting, easements, right-of-way coordination, and regulatory approvals.\n• Conduct site visits, field investigations, and construction support activities.\n• Mentor junior engineers while supporting project delivery, quality control, and client satisfaction.\n• Assist with proposals, statements of qualifications (SOQs), scopes of work, fee estimates, and project execution planning.","qualifications":"• Bachelor's degree in Civil Engineering, Environmental Engineering, or a related engineering discipline required.\n• Master's degree in Engineering preferred.\n• Colorado Professional Engineer (P.E.) license or the ability to obtain licensure within one year.\n• 5+ years of experience designing municipal water and wastewater infrastructure.\n• Experience in one or more of the following: Large-diameter pipelines Pump stations Lift stations Water treatment facilities Wastewater treatment facilities\n• Experience with project planning, design, and construction phase services.\n• Strong client relationship and project delivery skills.\n• Excellent communication, organizational, and technical problem-solving abilities.\nPreferred Experience:\n• Municipal utility projects.\n• Hydraulic modeling and system analysis.\n• Construction administration and field support.\n• Public agency coordination.\n• Multidisciplinary engineering project delivery.","whyConsider":"• Full-cycle water work: pipelines, pump stations and treatment plants, from planning through construction.\n• A full in-house bench, from civil and structural to MEP.\n• Water is one of the firm's core national markets, backed by in-house environmental and geospatial teams.\n• Mentorship by senior water engineers and a defined path to Senior PE and PM.\n• Decades of family ownership and steady, long-term leadership.\n• Work spans water, wastewater and infrastructure, so no two projects feel the same.\n• 401(k) match, tuition reimbursement and wellness programs.\n• Plus health insurance, PTO, and EIT/PE licensure support.","seoTitle":"Water / Wastewater Project Engineer – Pipelines, Pump Stations & Treatment | AGILE Position 1169","metaDescription":"Water / Wastewater Project Engineer – Pipelines, Pump Stations & Treatment in Denver, CO. Hybrid. Salary $100,000 to $120,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1170","responsibilities":"• Provide strategic leadership for complex land development projects from concept through construction.\n• Direct multidisciplinary project teams responsible for site design, grading, stormwater management, erosion control, utility design, and related engineering deliverables.\n• Oversee project scope, budgets, schedules, staffing, quality, risk management, and overall project performance.\n• Serve as the primary client advisor while developing long-term relationships and ensuring exceptional project delivery.\n• Guide projects through local, state, and federal permitting and regulatory approval processes.\n• Partner with department leadership to support business development initiatives, proposal development, and strategic client pursuits.\n• Identify opportunities to expand services with existing clients while supporting growth into new geographic and market sectors.\n• Provide technical leadership, mentor engineering professionals, and foster a collaborative culture focused on innovation, quality, and continuous improvement.","qualifications":"• Bachelor's degree in Civil Engineering or Landscape Architecture required.\n• 10+ years of experience managing land development and capital improvement projects.\n• North Carolina Professional Engineer (PE) or Registered Landscape Architect (RLA) license favored, or the ability to obtain within two months.\n• Proficiency with AutoCAD Civil 3D, stormwater modeling software, and Microsoft Office applications.\n• Demonstrated success leading multidisciplinary engineering teams while managing project budgets, schedules, and client relationships.\n• Strong understanding of permitting requirements and regulatory approval processes.\n• Excellent leadership, communication, and business development skills.\n• Proven ability to mentor technical staff while delivering high-quality engineering solutions.","whyConsider":"• Senior PM authority over the full land development lifecycle.\n• Multidisciplinary teams in-house, including a complete MEP consulting practice.\n• Energy, utility, residential, commercial and public clients in the Charlotte market.\n• Architecture, survey, environmental and engineering in-house.\n• Stable, family-owned leadership that plans for the long term.\n• Room to grow, with a structured path that shows exactly how to reach the next level.\n• Work keeps coming in, which means job security and new challenges each year.\n• Leadership development programs, tuition reimbursement and 401(k) match.\n• Health insurance and paid time off, with EIT and PE licensure support.","seoTitle":"Senior Civil Project Manager | AGILE Position 1170","metaDescription":"Senior Civil Project Manager in Charlotte, NC. Hybrid. Salary $140,000 to $165,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1171","responsibilities":"• Provide strategic project leadership for land development projects from concept through construction.\n• Lead multidisciplinary design teams responsible for site layout, grading, stormwater management, erosion control, utility design, and related engineering calculations and technical documentation.\n• Manage project scope, budgets, schedules, resources, quality, and overall project performance to ensure successful delivery.\n• Serve as a trusted client partner while building long-term relationships and delivering exceptional service throughout every phase of the project.\n• Coordinate permitting, project submittals, and regulatory approvals with local and state agencies.\n• Partner with department leadership to support business development initiatives, proposal preparation, marketing efforts, and strategic client pursuits.\n• Collaborate with multidisciplinary teams to expand services, strengthen existing client relationships, and deliver innovative engineering solutions.\n• Mentor junior and mid-level engineering professionals while fostering a collaborative culture focused on technical excellence and continuous improvement.","qualifications":"• Bachelor's degree in Civil Engineering or related engineering discipline preferred.\n• 6–10 years of experience in the design and management of land development and capital improvement projects.\n• North Carolina Professional Engineer (PE) or Registered Landscape Architect (RLA) license favored, or the ability to obtain North Carolina licensure within two months.\n• Proficiency with AutoCAD Civil 3D, stormwater modeling software, and Microsoft Office applications.\n• Demonstrated experience managing project budgets, schedules, and client relationships.\n• Strong understanding of permitting requirements, project submittals, and regulatory approval processes.\n• Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills.\n• Proven ability to provide technical leadership, mentor engineering staff, and successfully manage multidisciplinary project teams.","whyConsider":"• A PM seat with hands-on design ownership in the Charlotte market.\n• Work alongside civil, structural and MEP colleagues on integrated teams.\n• In-house survey, environmental and geospatial support on every project.\n• A clear track to Senior Project Manager, with formal leadership training.\n• A family-owned firm that values continuity and long careers.\n• Leadership invests in your progression, with a mapped route to your next role.\n• A robust pipeline of projects gives you stability and a steady stream of new challenges.\n• Broaden your portfolio across energy and utilities, residential, commercial, and government projects.\n• 401(k) with company match, tuition reimbursement and wellness programs.\n• Health insurance, paid time off, and EIT and PE licensure support.","seoTitle":"Site Civil Project Manager | AGILE Position 1171","metaDescription":"Site Civil Project Manager in Charlotte, NC. Hybrid. Salary $115,000 to $135,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1172","responsibilities":"• Design plumbing and fire protection systems, including domestic water, sanitary drainage & vent, storm drainage, pumping, natural gas distribution, and clean agent suppression systems\n• Perform system selections, prepare preliminary designs, and develop performance specifications\n• Consult on due diligence reviews, sustainability analyses, and feasibility studies\n• Incorporate design changes using AutoCAD and Revit\n• Execute design calculations to meet state/local code requirements; produce documentation aligned with client/project standards\n• Represent the firm in interactions with clients, contractors, architects, and team members\n• Provide technical leadership and mentor junior engineers/designers\n• Support delivery of both small and large-scale projects independently with minimal supervision","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s degree in Mechanical Engineering or related discipline (PE license highly preferred)\n• Minimum 4+ years plumbing/fire protection design experience; project management experience desirable\n• Strong knowledge of building codes, drafting standards, and plumbing/fire protection standards\n• Proficiency in AutoCAD and Revit\n• Understanding of construction processes and ability to interpret construction drawings\n• Working knowledge of diverse plumbing system applications\n• Strong communication and coordination skills with multi-disciplinary teams","whyConsider":"• Full-scope P&FP design, including clean-agent suppression and pumping systems.\n• A steady pipeline of school, campus, senior living and public work.\n• In-house architects and engineers for close, day-to-day coordination.\n• Growth toward senior technical and project leadership.\n• Comprehensive benefits, including a 401(k), health insurance, PTO, life and disability insurance, and EIT and PE licensure support.","seoTitle":"Project Engineer – Plumbing/Fire Protection | AGILE Position 1172","metaDescription":"Project Engineer – Plumbing/Fire Protection in Madison, NJ. Hybrid. Salary $105,000 to $125,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."}];
