   {"id":"1180","responsibilities":"• Lead site/civil design — grading, roadway design, storm water management, and erosion and sediment control — using Civil 3D\n• Serve as project manager responsible for client relationship management\n• Prepare calculations, reports, and spreadsheets\n• Collaborate with and manage design teams to develop detailed construction documents\n• Conduct code research, write specifications, and support permitting\n• Mentor entry-level staff","qualifications":"• B.S. in Civil Engineering required (Master’s preferred)\n• 6-10 years of experience\n• North Carolina PE license favored\n• Proficiency with AutoCAD, Civil 3D, and Microsoft Office\n• Strong written and verbal communication skills\n• Ability to communicate effectively with clients, sub-consultants, and agency review staff","whyConsider":"• Engineer and PM in one role, in the Research Triangle market.\n• A full in-house bench, from civil and structural to MEP.\n• Survey, environmental and architecture in-house.\n• A clear path to Senior PM, with formal leadership development.\n• Decades of family ownership and steady, long-term leadership.\n• A strong backlog, so you can focus on great work rather than the next assignment.\n• Work spans infrastructure, commercial, industrial, and government, so no two projects feel the same.\n• 401(k) match, tuition reimbursement and wellness programs.\n• Health insurance and paid time off, with EIT and PE licensure support.","seoTitle":"Civil Engineer/Project Manager – Raleigh, NC | AGILE Position 1180","metaDescription":"Civil Engineer/Project Manager in Raleigh, NC. 6-10 years of civil engineering experience. Salary $140,000 to $165,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."}
