-export default [{"id":"1181","responsibilities":"• Provide technical leadership and oversight for complex bridge design, rehabilitation, replacement, and transportation infrastructure projects\n• Serve as a senior technical resource for bridge engineering teams and provide guidance on design approaches, engineering solutions, and project delivery strategies\n• Lead QA/QC reviews of bridge plans, calculations, specifications, technical reports, and design documentation\n• Oversee structural analysis and design in accordance with AASHTO LRFD Bridge Design Specifications, NJDOT standards, and applicable agency requirements\n• Provide technical direction for bridge modeling, load rating analyses, structural evaluations, and rehabilitation design\n• Collaborate with roadway, traffic, geotechnical, environmental, hydraulic, and construction engineering professionals\n• Support complex project pursuits through technical strategy, proposals, interviews, and client presentations\n• Maintain and strengthen relationships with transportation agencies, municipalities, and public sector clients\n• Mentor and develop engineers within the Bridge Department\n• Help develop department standards, technical resources, and engineering best practices\n• Participate in strategic planning supporting continued growth of the transportation and bridge practice\n• Conduct site visits, bridge inspections, and field assessments as required","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s degree in Civil Engineering required\n• Master’s degree in Structural Engineering required\n• Professional Engineer (PE) license required\n• New Jersey, New York, and/or Pennsylvania PE preferred, or ability to obtain through reciprocity\n• 15+ years of progressive bridge design and structural engineering experience\n• Extensive experience delivering complex bridge and transportation infrastructure projects\n• Historical bridge design and rehabilitation experience is a plus\n• Advanced knowledge of AASHTO LRFD Bridge Design Specifications and NJDOT bridge design procedures\n• Strong expertise in bridge analysis, rehabilitation, replacement, and structural evaluation\n• Proficiency with bridge analysis and design software such as LEAP Bridge, LARSA, MIDAS, CSiBridge, STAAD, or equivalent programs\n• AutoCAD and/or MicroStation experience required\n• Demonstrated ability to provide technical leadership and mentor engineers\n• Strong communication, organization, collaboration, and problem solving skills\n• Established relationships with transportation agencies, municipalities, and public sector clients preferred\n• Business development, proposal preparation, and client engagement experience preferred","whyConsider":"This is much more than another senior bridge engineering position. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to help lead a respected Bridge Department working on major bridge replacements, rehabilitations, inspections, load ratings, staged construction, highway structures, historic bridges, waterfront and movable bridge projects, and other technically challenging infrastructure assignments throughout the region. The firm offers senior engineers meaningful access to project teams and decision making, providing the opportunity to influence engineering standards, mentor future leaders, and help shape the continued growth of the practice.\nAvailable now.","seoTitle":"Assistant Chief Engineer, Structural (Bridge) | AGILE Position 1181","metaDescription":"Assistant Chief Engineer, Structural (Bridge) in Wall Township, NJ. Salary $150,000 to $200,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1182","responsibilities":"• Perform structural analysis and design for new, rehabilitated, and replacement bridge and transportation structures\n• Prepare engineering calculations, design plans, technical reports, specifications, and project documentation\n• Develop structural models and perform analysis using bridge design software including LEAP Bridge, LARSA, MIDAS, CSiBridge, STAAD, or similar programs\n• Assist with bridge load ratings and structural evaluations\n• Coordinate design activities, project requirements, schedules, and deliverables\n• Collaborate with roadway, geotechnical, hydraulic, environmental, and construction engineering teams\n• Apply AASHTO LRFD Bridge Design Specifications, NJDOT standards, and applicable agency requirements\n• Participate in field visits, bridge inspections, and data collection\n• Review design documents for accuracy, quality, and project compliance\n• Support senior engineers with engineering solutions and technical activities\n• Assist with proposal preparation, cost estimating, and business development activities as needed","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s degree in Civil Engineering required\n• Master’s degree in Structural Engineering preferred\n• 5 to 8 years of progressive bridge design and structural engineering experience\n• Professional Engineer (PE) license favored\n• Experience with LEAP Bridge, LARSA, MIDAS, CSiBridge, STAAD, or equivalent bridge analysis and design software preferred\n• Proficiency with AutoCAD and/or MicroStation\n• Knowledge of AASHTO LRFD Bridge Design Specifications and NJDOT design procedures preferred\n• Strong analytical, problem solving, and technical communication skills\n• Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively within multidisciplinary project teams\n• Demonstrated interest in continued professional growth and development","whyConsider":"• Bridge design from analysis through documentation.\n• In-house geotechnical and materials testing, the firm's founding strength.\n• An ENR Top 500 firm every year, plus other industry rankings.\n• Senior bridge engineers to learn from, and a path to Senior Project Engineer.\n• On-site in Wall Township. Talk with us first; your search stays private.\n• Work keeps coming in, which means job security and new challenges each year.\n• Broaden your portfolio across transportation and infrastructure projects.\n• Benefits include a 401(k), health insurance, paid time off, life and disability insurance, and EIT and PE licensure support.","seoTitle":"Structural Project Engineer – Bridge | AGILE Position 1182","metaDescription":"Structural Project Engineer – Bridge in Wall Township, NJ. Salary $90,000 to $115,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."},{"id":"1183","responsibilities":"• Lead and manage complex transportation and infrastructure projects from planning and concept development through final design, permitting, bidding, and construction support\n• Manage bridge rehabilitation, bridge replacement, roadway, highway, transportation infrastructure, and related municipal improvement projects\n• Lead multidisciplinary teams across bridge, roadway, traffic, geotechnical, environmental, water resources, and related engineering disciplines\n• Serve as a primary client contact for NJDOT, counties, municipalities, and other transportation agencies\n• Manage project scope, schedules, budgets, staffing, quality control, and client expectations\n• Oversee engineering plans, specifications, cost estimates, technical reports, calculations, and project documentation\n• Provide technical leadership on transportation and structural engineering solutions and project delivery strategies\n• Coordinate design activities and resolve technical issues affecting project schedules and deliverables\n• Ensure compliance with applicable AASHTO, NJDOT, MUTCD, local agency, and related requirements\n• Conduct site visits, field investigations, inspections, and structural assessments as needed\n• Mentor and develop junior and mid level engineers\n• Participate in proposals, scope and fee preparation, client presentations, interviews, and business development initiatives\n• Identify opportunities to expand client relationships and support continued practice growth","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s degree in Civil Engineering required\n• Master’s degree in Structural Engineering or 