otiations, presentations, and interview teams\n• Develop and maintain a strong project backlog and support the financial performance and utilization of the Transportation Group\n• Monitor staffing, workload, utilization, and project assignments\n• Recruit, retain, mentor, and develop engineers and Project Managers\n• Establish career development opportunities and succession plans for key team members\n• Promote collaboration across Highway, Traffic, Bridge, Civil, Geotechnical, Environmental, Water Resources, and Construction Engineering groups\n• Provide technical oversight and quality assurance for transportation projects\n• Participate in strategic planning and provide leadership insight on market conditions, staffing requirements, client needs, and growth opportunities","qualifications":"• Bachelor’s degree in Civil Engineering required\n• Master’s degree in Civil, Transportation, Structural Engineering, or a related discipline preferred\n• Professional Engineer (PE) license favored\n• New Jersey PE preferred or ability to obtain through reciprocity\n• Minimum 15 years of progressive transportation, highway, traffic, bridge, structural, or related infrastructure consulting experience\n• Demonstrated experience managing complex transportation projects through planning, design, permitting, bidding, and construction\n• Strong background in Highway, Traffic, Bridge, or a combination of these disciplines\n• Experience leading engineering teams and managing multiple Project Managers and technical professionals\n• Proven ability to develop and maintain relationships with transportation agencies and public sector clients\n• Strong understanding of project management, financial performance, staffing, quality control, and risk management\n• Demonstrated success in business development, proposals, client presentations, and strategic account management\n• Strong leadership, mentoring, recruiting, and staff development capabilities\n• Strong understanding of the New Jersey transportation market and public sector procurement\n• Experience leading a Highway, Traffic, and Bridge practice or group is highly desirable\n• Existing transportation client relationships and demonstrated ability to develop a strong project backlog are highly desirable","whyConsider":"• Group-level leadership: you own the strategy and the team.\n• Ranked in ENR's Top 500 every year, plus other national industry rankings.\n• Leadership invested in growing the firm's next leaders.\n• Geotechnical, structural and land development partners in-house.\n• On-site in Wall Township. Start with a private conversation through us.\n• A defined promotion path, with regular conversations about where you're headed next.\n• A strong project pipeline means steady, meaningful work and the stability to build a long-term career.\n• Build a well-rounded résumé across transportation and infrastructure work.\n• Comprehensive benefits, including a 401(k), health insurance, PTO, life and disability insurance, and EIT and PE licensure support.","seoTitle":"Transportation Group Manager | AGILE Position 1185","metaDescription":"Transportation Group Manager in Wall Township, NJ. Salary $175,000 to $225,000. Review confidential career details from AGILE."}];
