-export default [{"id": "1212", "responsibilities": "• Serve as technical lead and project manager for electrical design on commercial, industrial, and institutional facilities and rail stations\n• Lead design of medium and low voltage power distribution (480V–15kV), lighting and lighting controls, emergency/standby power and generators, fire alarm, lightning protection, and grounding systems\n• Manage projects with teams of 2–3 engineers and electrical construction costs in the $1M–$8M range\n• Prepare electrical design drawings and specifications\n• Conduct site visits and field inspections, and prepare assessment reports of electrical systems\n• Coordinate the work of multiple disciplines and work directly with clients\n• Mentor junior engineers technically and professionally", "qualifications": "• Bachelor of Science in Electrical Engineering (BSEE) from an ABET-accredited university\n• 10–15+ years of electrical engineering design and construction support experience\n• Professional Engineer (PE) license in New York or New Jersey favored\n• In-depth knowledge of NYC, New York State, and national codes and standards\n• Proven success as a senior project-level engineer with electrical project management experience\n• Experience working with Con Edison and other electric utilities\n• Proficiency with electrical engineering software such as Visual Lighting, AGI32, and SKM Power Systems Analysis\n• AutoCAD and Revit experience preferred; experience managing BIM/Revit production a plus\n• Proficiency with Microsoft Word, PowerPoint, Outlook, and Excel\n• Valid driver’s license and clean driving record required\n• Must be authorized to work in the U.S. without sponsorship", "whyConsider": "• Technical lead and PM on medium-voltage and rail station work, a rare combination.\n• A full MEP consulting practice inside a national civil, transportation and infrastructure firm, so building systems work comes with big-firm backing.\n• Transit and infrastructure clients backed b